Z||000002||c m west||02-09-2001||01:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CHOWITT31:<BR><B>Hi folks on my way to work this afternoon my TCC started to kick in and out and eventualy thru a code wich turned out to be a code 22.<BR>Now this same thing happened about a week ago but it disappeared.<BR>Anyway, has this problem ever happened to any of you folks and if so what was the fix.<BR>It looks like I will have to replace the TPS.<BR>Comments and opinions welcome.<BR>Thanks<BR>ken</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> spmetimes the tab from the tbs that is moved<BR>by the throttle lever gets bent and distorted over time, I have found that at idle you want the voltage at 0.76 V from the TPS and a steady increase to in between 4.75 V and 4.95 V. Also this is one cade that can be set of by a stuck thermostat ( engine computer delivers more fuel in attempt to "warm-up" the engine, as well as the cause for most O2, and EGR codes.<P>||||reg||10
